            <ArticleTitle>New Health Technologies: A UK Perspective Comment on &quot;Providing Value to New Health Technology: The Early Contribution of Entrepreneurs, Investors, and Regulatory Agencies&quot;.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>721-722</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.15171/ijhpm.2017.59</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>New health technologies require development and evaluation ahead of being incorporated into the patient care pathway. In light of the recent publication by Lehoux et al who discuss the role of entrepreneurs, investors and regulators in providing value to new health technologies, we summarise the processes involved in making new health technologies available for use in the United Kingdom.</AbstractText>
